        "original_id": "5b9cc7a5-a6ed-55c7-961f-23a598dedfd2",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: 2001 Asian Junior Athletics Championships\n- Organizations: Asian Athletics Association\n- Sports disciplines: 3000 metres steeplechase, steeplechase\n- People: Mekdes Bekele Tadese\n- Topics: Asian under-20 athletics, track and field\n\nFacts:\n- The 2001 Asian Junior Athletics Championships was the ninth edition of an international athletics competition for Asian under-20 athletes.\n- The Asian Athletics Association organised the 2001 Asian Junior Athletics Championships.\n- A total of 43 events were contested at the 2001 Asian Junior Athletics Championships.\n- The 2001 Asian Junior Athletics Championships divided events equally between male and female athletes except for the men's 3000 metres steeplechase.\n- The 3000 metres steeplechase is the most common steeplechase distance in track and field.\n- The 3000 metres steeplechase is an obstacle race run over 3000 metres.\n- The steeplechase derives its name from horse racing steeplechase.\n- Mekdes Bekele Tadese, born on 20 January 1987, is an Ethiopian runner who specializes in the 3000 metres steeplechase.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "cb2d6a7b-613a-5202-8bca-ce495c1ad519",
        "text": "Page: 2001 Asian Junior Athletics Championships. Sentence: The 2001 Asian Junior Athletics Championships was the ninth edition of the international athletics competition for Asian under-20 athletes, organised by the Asian Athletics Association.\nPage: 2001 Asian Junior Athletics Championships. Sentence: A total of 43 events were contested, which were divided equally between male and female athletes aside from the men's 3000 metres steeplechase.\nPage: 3000 metres steeplechase. Sentence: The 3000 metres steeplechase or 3000-meter steeplechase is the most common distance for the steeplechase in track and field.\nPage: 3000 metres steeplechase. Sentence: It is an obstacle race over the distance of the 3000 metres, which derives its name from the horse racing steeplechase.\nPage: Mekdes Bekele. Sentence: Mekdes Bekele Tadese (Amharic: መቅደስ በቀለ ታደሰ; born 20 January 1987) is an Ethiopian runner who specializes in the 3000 metres steeplechase.",
